      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "+1 for this.  It would be really great to be able to take advantage of the things humanoid rigs can do without having to do weird rigging magic to force it to work as humanoid.  Right now generic rigs can't use :  Speech Visemes, Gesture Overrides, Chairs (sit), Emotes, Menu if viewball is too low, animation overrides for non-walk/idle motions (unless I just suck at animation states), crouch/prone poses (just moves the viewball up and down).   I'm probably forgetting something else that's broken.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
